source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-24
observed: A row's own opening delimiter decides its cells however many lines it takes: `||h` opens a header row, and Jira renders one header cell holding `h`, a break and `x`.
-- input.jira --
||h
x||
|a|
-- rendered.html --
<div class='table-wrap'>
<table class='confluenceTable'><tbody>
<tr>
<th class='confluenceTh'>h<br/>
x</th>
</tr>
<tr>
<td class='confluenceTd'>a</td>
</tr>
</tbody></table>
</div>
-- want.md --
:::table
||h
x||
|a|
:::
-- warnings.json --
[]
